        "text": "| 1 | \"the raw material from which a self is assembled\" / \"not selling minutes … selling portions of a person\" | **Metapher**（Ökonomie-Wortfeld：commodity, market, stockpiled, priced, transaction） | 把抽象的注意力变成可切割、可出售的物体，读者立刻感到「被当成货物」的冒犯，These 因此有了画面感。 |  *Die Metaphorik des Marktes überträgt die Logik des Warentauschs auf das Subjekt selbst.*<br> *By using market imagery — \"raw material\", \"portions of a person\" — the author turns an abstract resource into something that can be cut up and sold, which makes his thesis immediately tangible.* |",
