        "kind": "p",
        "text": "| 2 | \"It is not selling minutes. It is selling portions of a person.\" / \"A mirror shows you your face; a prediction engine shows you …\" | **Antithese**（mit Parallelismus） | 两句结构对称、语义相对，制造「看似/实是」的落差，读者被迫放弃原有理解，接受作者的重构。 |  *Die Antithese zwingt den Leser, die gängige Deutung aufzugeben und die des Autors zu übernehmen.*<br> *Through the antithesis of \"mirror\" and \"prediction engine\", the author dismantles the common defence that algorithms are neutral.* |",
